  "historical_output_text": " \n\nPhotosynthesis:\nPhotosynthesis is the process by which plants, algae, and some bacteria convert light energy into chemical energy to fuel their growth and survival. At its core, the process captures sunlight, uses water and carbon dioxide, and produces glucose and oxygen.\n\nThe process occurs in two main stages: the light-dependent reactions and the light-independent reactions (also known as the Calvin cycle). \n\nLight-dependent reactions happen in the thylakoid membranes of chloroplasts. Chlorophyll pigments absorb sunlight, exciting electrons to a higher energy state. These excited electrons are passed through a series of proteins and molecules, eventually reducing NADP",
